title: The same call, from two identities
subtitle: Same code, same subnets, same security group. One attribute differs.
width: 1120
---
Both callers are Lambda functions in the SAME VPC, the SAME two subnets,
behind the SAME security group, running BYTE-IDENTICAL code. Both are
granted vpc-lattice-svcs:Invoke by their own IAM policy.

The only difference is the role attached to the function.

$ aws lambda invoke --function-name week23-lattice-client \
      --payload '{"mode":"signed","method":"GET","path":"/rates"}'

  status: 200                                                        [ok]
  {"service": "rates", "method": "GET", "rate": 42.5,
   "note": "this function performed no authorisation of its own"}

$ aws lambda invoke --function-name week23-lattice-intruder \
      --payload '{"mode":"signed","method":"GET","path":"/rates"}'

  status: 403                                                        [ok]
  AccessDeniedException: User:
    arn:aws:sts::<account>:assumed-role/week23-lattice-stranger/...
  is not authorized to perform: vpc-lattice-svcs:Invoke

--- and the right caller, using a method the policy does not allow ---------

$ aws lambda invoke --function-name week23-lattice-client \
      --payload '{"mode":"signed","method":"POST","path":"/rates"}'

  status: 403                                                        [ok]
  arn:aws:sts::<account>:assumed-role/week23-lattice-orders-client/...
  is not authorized to perform: vpc-lattice-svcs:Invoke

--- and an unsigned caller -------------------------------------------------

  status: 403                                                        [ok]
  User: anonymous ... because no NETWORK-BASED policy allows the
  vpc-lattice-svcs:Invoke action

Note the wording of that last one. It names which of the two layers
refused -- the service network policy, not the service policy. That
distinction becomes important in the next figure.

A security group cannot produce these four different answers. It sees one
subnet, one set of rules, and four identical packets.
